{
  "description": "Overview ranks accounts before applying any filter: expired sign-in first, then ADR 0002 headline percent left (exhausted = zero, missing figure last), then creation time and Unicode scalar ID. All keeps that entire rank; Needs attention keeps only reconnectRequired; Resets today keeps accounts with any recorded reset strictly between now and the start of the next local day in the given IANA zone, regardless of connection, reading validity or window scope. The header attention count is over all usage accounts. Its reset is the earliest recorded reset strictly after now across connected accounts and all windows, even beyond today. Header kind: attention when the count is positive, room when the nonempty register has no expired sign-ins and every ADR 0002 headline is current, known, non-exhausted and strictly above 20% left; a usable paused/partial reading can qualify. Otherwise resetOnly if there is a header reset, none if not. attention and room can carry an optional reset too. A headline is not current when the reading failed, age is at least staleAfterMs, or its reset fell due since measurement. No render text is tested. Expected answers are handwritten.",
  "schema": "vectors: array of { name, zone: IANA ID, zoneRule: string or null, now: epoch ms, staleAfterMs: duration ms, accounts: stored-order array of { id, createdAt: epoch ms, connection: connected|reconnectRequired|unknown, pauseUntil: epoch ms or null, reading: null or { fetchedAt: epoch ms, status: ok|partial|failed, windows: [{ id, scope: global|model|unknown, remainingPercent: number or null, exhausted: boolean, resetAt: epoch ms or null }] in provider order } }, expected: { visible: { all: [ID], needsAttention: [ID], resetsToday: [ID] }, attentionCount: integer, header: { kind: attention|room|resetOnly|none, resetAt: epoch ms or null } } }. All keys must be present, including nullable ones.",
